This project incorporates and builds upon code and polyfills originating from
multiple open-source projects. All adapted components are redistributed under
their respective permissive open-source licenses (predominantly MIT and BSD-style).

1. WasmEdge-QuickJS (Modules Framework)
   - Original Repository: https://github.com/second-state/wasmedge-quickjs
   - Fork / Upstream Base: https://github.com/Mahavishnu-K/wasmedge-quickjs
   - Copyright (c) Second State INC and contributors.
   - License: MIT License
   - Modifications by Mahavishnu K <https://github.com/Mahavishnu-K>:
     * Severed all proprietary WasmEdge host bindings (_node:os, _node:crypto,
       custom WASI socket extensions).
     * Re-engineered module loaders to execute inside vanilla Wasmtime (WASI Preview 1).
     * Rebuilt the filesystem (fs.js) and process (process.js) modules to rely
       strictly on QuickJS built-in C APIs ('std' and 'os').
     * Implemented VFS portals (.ore_crypto and .ore_network) for hardware-accelerated
       cryptography and zero-RAM disk-streaming network fetch.
     * Rewrote module imports with explicit POSIX '.js' extensions to prevent
       QuickJS literal fopen() resolution errors.
     * Decoupled circular dependency deadlocks and eliminated top-level await in
       foundational modules.

